487
00:25:55.472 --> 00:25:58.225
Yeah, sure. Lovely to meet you.

488
00:25:59.768 --> 00:26:01.061
She your new girlfriend?

489
00:26:01.144 --> 00:26:04.773
Relax, babe.
It's all part of the branding plan, innit?

490
00:26:04.857 --> 00:26:07.776
If I've got two women bidding on me,
it makes me look more valuable.

491
00:26:07.860 --> 00:26:08.944
Do you know what I mean?

492
00:26:09.778 --> 00:26:10.988
It's fucking smart, eh?

493
00:26:11.697 --> 00:26:17.452
And now, the only former Champions League
winner on the menu, say hello to Roy Kent.

494
00:26:17.536 --> 00:26:18.579
Granddad.

495
00:26:21.081 --> 00:26:26.336
And the highest bidder gets to spend
a day at a swanky hotel by the pool

496
00:26:26.420 --> 00:26:29.965
drinking frozen daiquiris
and soaking up the rays--

497
00:26:30.048 --> 00:26:32.259
No, we said
there's no daiquiris and no rays.

498
00:26:34.094 --> 00:26:37.306
There's not gonna be a fucking pool
either. We're not leaving SW14.

499
00:26:37.389 --> 00:26:40.058
You looked so jealous. It was so cool.

500
00:26:40.142 --> 00:26:42.019
You think jealousy is cool, do you?

501
00:26:42.102 --> 00:26:43.604
Don't know, babe. I don't get jealous.

502
00:26:43.687 --> 00:26:47.065
Well, can we have 100 quid for what's
turning out to be a very boring date?

503
00:26:47.524 --> 00:26:48.859
All right. A thousand pounds.

504
00:26:50.319 --> 00:26:53.739
-Any advances on that?
-Two thousand pounds!

505
00:26:54.865 --> 00:26:57.075
Cheryl's got fire inside her.

506
00:26:57.159 --> 00:27:00.078
-Three thousand pounds.
-Babe, you're just embarrassing yourself.

507
00:27:00.704 --> 00:27:02.623
Four thousand pounds!

508
00:27:02.706 --> 00:27:03.790
Five thousand!

509
00:27:04.541 --> 00:27:06.835
Six thousand pounds.

510
00:27:06.919 --> 00:27:08.879
-Any advance on six?
-I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

511
00:27:10.088 --> 00:27:12.049
Okay, sold to Cheryl.

512
00:27:19.723 --> 00:27:24.728
That concludes the auction,
apart from one small surprise.

513
00:27:25.604 --> 00:27:31.527
I am personally donating
£1 million to the cause.

514
00:27:34.154 --> 00:27:35.155
Thank you.

515
00:27:35.656 --> 00:27:37.449
Thank you very much. Thank you.

516
00:27:37.533 --> 00:27:43.705
And that, I believe, gets Rebecca
over her goal of 800,000. Thank you.

517
00:27:47.459 --> 00:27:48.794
For the children, eh?

518
00:28:00.556 --> 00:28:01.640
Rebecca.

519
00:28:01.723 --> 00:28:05.644
This here is Cam Cole.
He's an undiscovered mega-talent.

520
00:28:05.727 --> 00:28:07.187
Go on, Cam. Show 'em what you got.

521
00:28:11.441 --> 00:28:12.442
Are you insane?

522
00:28:12.526 --> 00:28:16.488
Hey, Rebecca. You do not wanna judge
this book by its cover right here, okay?

523
00:28:17.865 --> 00:28:18.866
The hell with it.

524
00:28:20.617 --> 00:28:21.618
Yes.

525
00:28:22.911 --> 00:28:27.916
Hello again. Ladies and gentlemen,
I regret to inform you that...

526
00:28:29.209 --> 00:28:33.297
Robbie Williams is unable to be here
tonight due to an emergency.

527
00:28:33.380 --> 00:28:38.218
But we have a brilliant replacement
for you who you are just going to love.

528
00:28:38.302 --> 00:28:41.180
Or, at least, have lots to talk about
on the way home.

529
00:28:41.972 --> 00:28:47.603
All the way from outside...
please welcome Cam something.

530
00:28:54.818 --> 00:28:56.111
Bollocks.

531
00:28:57.696 --> 00:28:58.697
What does that mean?

532
00:29:12.961 --> 00:29:18.592
<i>Mama, sweet mama nature
Please forgive us and what we've done</i>

533
00:29:21.553 --> 00:29:23.889
Can we just forget about the game
and go and have a dance?

534
00:29:24.598 --> 00:29:26.683
Queen to king five. Checkmate.

535
00:29:33.815 --> 00:29:36.777
<i>We've gone and hurt our mama</i>

536
00:29:36.860 --> 00:29:40.072
<i>And her wrath has begun</i>

537
00:30:02.970 --> 00:30:06.014
<i>'Cause I'm a good boy to my mama</i>

538
00:30:09.101 --> 00:30:13.814
<i>But</i>

539
00:30:13.897 --> 00:30:19.027
<i>I've got bad siblings</i>

540
00:30:27.536 --> 00:30:29.121
-Thank you so much.
-You're so welcome.

541
00:30:29.204 --> 00:30:31.248
-We really had a great time.
-Thank you so much.

542
00:30:32.291 --> 00:30:33.417
Good night.

543
00:30:33.959 --> 00:30:36.670
Thank you again
for such an unbelievable donation.

544
00:30:36.753 --> 00:30:38.505
-See you again next year.
-Can't wait.

545
00:30:45.470 --> 00:30:46.680
What a charmer, huh?

546
00:30:47.347 --> 00:30:48.390
Indeed.

547
00:30:51.268 --> 00:30:55.189
You may think that you're the only one
that can see who he really is...

548
00:30:56.690 --> 00:30:57.691
but you're not.

549
00:31:04.823 --> 00:31:06.325
Oh, boy. You all right, buddy?

550
00:31:08.410 --> 00:31:10.245
-Quick.
-All right.

551
00:31:10.329 --> 00:31:11.330
Fun night.

552
00:31:12.915 --> 00:31:15.125
Hey, wait, hold on. Slow down, Coach.

553
00:31:19.171 --> 00:31:20.964
Will you stop being mad at me now?

554
00:31:24.009 --> 00:31:25.219
I'm sorry, babe.

555
00:31:27.638 --> 00:31:29.598
Do you even know
what you're sorry for, Jamie?

556
00:31:30.474 --> 00:31:31.600
You always ask me that.

557
00:31:32.392 --> 00:31:34.520
Hey, do me a favor.

558
00:31:34.603 --> 00:31:36.605
Don't use me as a prop
in your little fights.

559
00:31:37.564 --> 00:31:38.732
Made me feel like an idiot.

560
00:31:41.068 --> 00:31:42.903
I'm sorry. I--

561
00:31:43.445 --> 00:31:44.655
I shouldn't have done that.

562
00:31:45.906 --> 00:31:46.907
Thanks.

563
00:31:47.533 --> 00:31:49.868
No one was bidding on you anyway, mate.
Just fuck off.

564
00:31:51.411 --> 00:31:52.412
Go on.

565
00:31:56.667 --> 00:31:58.210
What are you saying sorry to him for?

566
00:31:58.710 --> 00:32:00.712
Being accountable matters, Jamie.

567
00:32:03.674 --> 00:32:04.675
We're done.

568
00:32:06.093 --> 00:32:07.094
I'll see you around.

569
00:32:10.931 --> 00:32:11.932
Whatever.

570
00:32:18.438 --> 00:32:20.566
Excuse me, can I take these?

571
00:32:20.649 --> 00:32:21.650
Two?

572
00:32:31.451 --> 00:32:33.120
Do you wanna go get, like, really drunk?

573
00:32:33.537 --> 00:32:36.248
-Yes, I do.
-Then we can go rob a bank or something.

574
00:32:43.005 --> 00:32:45.048
Michelle and Henry
are coming out next weekend.

575
00:32:45.132 --> 00:32:46.508
-Hey, that's great, Coach.
-Yeah.

576
00:32:47.217 --> 00:32:49.511
So come on, tell me about you and Jane.
What happened?

577
00:32:50.095 --> 00:32:51.221
I did it again.

578
00:32:51.305 --> 00:32:54.016
-Put the game before the dame, huh?
-Yup.

579
00:32:54.099 --> 00:32:55.809
When are you gonna learn, Coach?

